of the Pendragon Line in my Mage Game and it's brought a fantastic addition to the cast. Thank you so much for your work on these, it's all very inspiring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T18:30:18-07:00","id":761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=747#post747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say that I'm using a member of the Pendragon Line in my Mage Game and it's brought a fantastic addition to the cast. Thank you so much for your work on these, it's all very inspiring.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's wonderful to hear. Any fascinating stories to tell? Questions to clear up? Feedback is a marvelous thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. Should I take this as a, &quot;write more Pendragon Blessings plz&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T19:15:07-07:00","id":787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=761#post761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's wonderful to hear. Any fascinating stories to tell? Questions to clear up? Feedback is a marvelous thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. Should I take this as a, &quot;write more Pendragon Blessings plz&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, totally!<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about their Curse, which I think is an interesting one. My issue is that the player who is a Pendragon is an Awakened Pendragon, so I wasn't sure what level of Blessings to give her.<br /> <br /> We've been negotiating it as her having the Second Blessing, but I do DESPERATELY want to introduce family members that are proper Proximi, so more Blessings are something I'm terrifically keen on.<br /> <br /> I also was wondering if you had any suggestions for what Legacy might be the Pendragon Legacy? I've been wondering which one you might recommend from the pre-existing ones.<br /> <br /> Since we didn't have a solid suggestion though, we've taken to crafting our own. The idea behind the Legacy is that they're really focused on the weapon they use, consecrating a chosen weapon which is the only weapon that the Attainments (Which are primarily Matter/Prime) then enhance.<br /> <br /> I won't lie, if I was a player and not the GM, I'd take on the interesting and fun challenge of playing a Proximi rather than an Awakened character. Besides, I could always Awaken later.<br /> <br /> If you have some suggestions for how to distribute blessing dots, if any for a Proximi that Awakened after starting, I'd love to hear them. I was just concerned about how to approach it because I was misunderstanding the blessings they had as following a strict ascending hierarchy like a discipline. I definitely think throwing some additional examples in there for the first Proximi Dynasty anybody reads about would help get the idea across that they're not like that.<br /> <br /> They're also just really awesome ideas in general, all of the Blessings. My hat goes off to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T16:00:56-07:00","id":1345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=787#post787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, totally!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Urxj0z6zvILm6-RAdUWXi5X_M6ppIjQ54H2Cb_prQM/edit#heading=h.dp2ecp2y40hf\" target=\"_blank\">Bam. Eight more blessings</a>. I can't seem to update the main post, otherwise I'd make note of it in the change log.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=787#post787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking about their Curse, which I think is an interesting one. My issue is that the player who is a Pendragon is an Awakened Pendragon, so I wasn't sure what level of Blessings to give her.<br /> <br /> We've been negotiating it as her having the Second Blessing, but I do DESPERATELY want to introduce family members that are proper Proximi, so more Blessings are something I'm terrifically keen on.<br /> <br /> If you have some suggestions for how to distribute blessing dots, if any for a Proximi that Awakened after starting, I'd love to hear them. I was just concerned about how to approach it because I was misunderstanding the blessings they had as following a strict ascending hierarchy like a discipline. I definitely think throwing some additional examples in there for the first Proximi Dynasty anybody reads about would help get the idea across that they're not like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, the rules for Awakened Proximi do kinda assume that such characters would awaken through play. Meaning that they'd awaken only after gaining a fair amount of exp. A Proximi who awakens shortly after unlocking her powers won't have had time to learn many Blessings or grow her Arete.<br /> <br /> What you could do, if you are not using starting characters, is have the player build as a Proximi and then, as the last step after making the character, apply the awakened template. The character probably wouldn't have as many Arcana dots as others to start, but she'd have Pendragon Blessings to fall back on that'd give her a clear advantage in certain scenarios (i.e. Combat). At the very least she'd start with three Blessings, as per the Proximi creation rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=787#post787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also was wondering if you had any suggestions for what Legacy might be the Pendragon Legacy? I've been wondering which one you might recommend from the pre-existing ones.<br /> <br /> Since we didn't have a solid suggestion though, we've taken to crafting our own. The idea behind the Legacy is that they're really focused on the weapon they use, consecrating a chosen weapon which is the only weapon that the Attainments (Which are primarily Matter/Prime) then enhance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't written one as I don't have any Awakened Pendragon in my games, but yours sounds like its on the right track. The easy way would be to pick a few blessings and convert them into Attainments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=787#post787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't lie, if I was a player and not the GM, I'd take on the interesting and fun challenge of playing a Proximi rather than an Awakened character. Besides, I could always Awaken later.<br /> <br /> They're also just really awesome ideas in general, all of the Blessings. My hat goes off to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proximi are probably the most fit of the sub-splats in this project to play among awakened characters. Their Blessings are deliberately very powerful, and while Proximi aren't as flexible as Mages, they generally run about a dot ahead in terms of sheer spell-power in their area of expertise.<br /> <br /> Plus I find that power inequality is fine in a game. Just so long as everyone is enjoying the power they have, and characters are given sufficient moments to shine (And Proximi can really shine)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-02-2013, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T16:38:54-08:00","id":2162,"title":"","content":"This is... Extremely cool actually. I really love this. <br /> Seeing as you picked up the Thaumaturges from Second Sight, do you have any intention to bake in the Psychics from that book as well? My initial reaction is that they'd fit quite well in with the Guardians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T00:22:39-08:00","id":2454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=2162#post2162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is... Extremely cool actually. I really love this.<br /> Seeing as you picked up the Thaumaturges from Second Sight, do you have any intention to bake in the Psychics from that book as well? My initial reaction is that they'd fit quite well in with the Guardians.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was not my intention to include psychics, especially since GMC has done such a good job of supporting them with Supernatural Merits. The Sub-groups here are more an exploration of how sleepwalkers can interact with Awakened Magic, and the different way magic is classically acquired. Though, that said, I'd venture that the Mysterium has a keen interest in psychics as a source of insight, and the Adamant Arrow looks on them as potential allies. Not certain if the Guardians would be fond of them, it'd likely have to be evaluated case-by-case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T15:45:10-08:00","id":2959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=2454#post2454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was not my intention to include psychics, especially since GMC has done such a good job of supporting them with Supernatural Merits. The Sub-groups here are more an exploration of how sleepwalkers can interact with Awakened Magic, and the different way magic is classically acquired. Though, that said, I'd venture that the Mysterium has a keen interest in psychics as a source of insight, and the Adamant Arrow looks on them as potential allies. Not certain if the Guardians would be fond of them, it'd likely have to be evaluated case-by-case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you are probably right. The Psychics = Guardians was more of a knee-jerk reaction when I read your stuff, based on the logic that the psychic can use his powers and often remain unnoticed, and it has mind control, something I at least associate tightly with the Guardians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T17:56:59-08:00","id":3058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=2959#post2959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you are probably right. The Psychics = Guardians was more of a knee-jerk reaction when I read your stuff, based on the logic that the psychic can use his powers and often remain unnoticed, and it has mind control, something I at least associate tightly with the Guardians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm certainly not claiming that Guardians wouldn't employ Psychics, they'd reasonably employ anyone of sound mind, like philosophy, and willing to take personal responsibility. And I think psychics would be right at home in a half-awake game, more versatile than Proximi, more immediate than Thaumaturges, and not dependent on others like Imbued, Occulted, or Thaumatech Adopters. Though you can judge that for yourself when those sections are finished.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though as I re-read them I'm starting to think they'd fit pretty well with the Mysterium...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-04-2013, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T14:24:31-08:00","id":6331,"title":"","content":"Quick project update, as I can no longer alter the main post (which is a huge inconvenience).<ul><li>The Pendragon Line and House Telyavel have been updated with new Blessings, bringing each up to 13 Blessings total.</li> <li>Thaumaturges is coming along nicely. I completely ditched major sections of my previous draft and reworked their Sphere structure. I'll post it up in the near future, though I still don't know what I'll do about the outdated hub post problem...</li> </ul>Here's a little spoiler of how Thaumaturges look now:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Scholars of Urd</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Origin: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Early in the 18th century the Mysterium began an experiment, an attempt to enlighten mortals by through Atlantean education. Sleepwalkers were taught Atlantean runes and phrases in high speech, the hope being that through arcane language the unawakened would connect with the Tellurian. But alas, try as they may Sleepwalkers could not see the higher meaning of the mystic language and, less than a decade after its conception, Mages abandoned the project. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">But the Sleepwalkers did not. Bereft of awakened guidance scholars continued to puzzle over runes. They branched out, pulling in symbols from other disciplines and inventing some of their own. Then something uncanny happened, the scholars succeeded. But the magic they unlocked was not that of Atlantis, indeed to awakened eyes the runic arrangements appeared to be nonsense. A random jumble of symbols arranged in an aesthetically pleasing manner. Whatever the sages saw, it was not the Tellurian. Despite concerns of abyssal intrusion, the Scholars of Urd were quickly reincorporated into the Mysterium curriculum, and remain a hot topic of study and debate to this day.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">College Structure: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">More so than any other curriculum the Scholars of Urd operate as a true college. Newcomers are given shadow names, divided into classes, and awarded degrees for achievement. Experienced Sages hold seminars, lectures, and experiments in runecraft. In a perfect world Sages would operative in an environment of unrestricted learning and creativity. The World of Darkness is far from perfect. Regimented curriculums are impersonal, academics is weighed down by politics, and experienced sages covet their findings, restricting their full knowledge to favorite apprentices. Magical genius alone will not take an aspiring sage to the top, they\u2019ll require a healthy amount of political savvy and ruthless politic to master the runic arts.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ritual: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rune Magic. Before a Sage can work her arts she must first scribe the runes necessary for her spell. Because every spell uses radically different incantations, and runic arrangements are in no way interchangeable, rune magic tends to require a great deal of preparation. Sages prepare their spells in advance, and store arrangements on spellbooks, scrolls, and tablets. Failing that the only option is to scribe runes by hand, a time consuming process.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This requires an extended Intelligence + Academics roll, with a target of three times the sorcery\u2019s dot rating and an interval of one roll every ten minutes. Storytellers can reasonably wave this roll when the Sage is unharried, but when the pressure is on setting up rune magic can be difficult. Should the runes that maintain a spell ever be damaged in any way the spell ceases instantly, which makes rune magic a tad unreliable in violent conflict.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Style: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rune magic is a </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">vulgar </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">art. The sorceries of the sages do not operate quietly, they </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">command</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">warp</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">control </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">reality at its very core. Rune magic is never covert or incidental, when a Sage throws lightning she does so by conjuring it from the runes at her feet, when she makes a portal it manifests as a shimmering gateway floating mid air. Even spells that would normally be covert take on obviously magical properties, tass glows bright red, shields spark and flicker, and scrying creates floating eyes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Spheres: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Abjuration, Conjuration, Transmutation</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Abjuration is the art of shielding and protection. Sorceries create armor, protect areas from intrusion, and forge magical prisons.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Conjuration creates and summons. Sorceries fling lightning, forge phantasms, and connect distant locations.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Transmutations deals in transformation of matter and energy. Sorceries turn lead to gold, convert mana to tass, and alter the base properties of material.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Intelligence + Sphere</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sample Sorceries: </span></b></span></span><ul><li><b><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Abjuration </span></i></b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">- Counterspell (Any) \u2022, Dispel Magic \u2022, Unseen Shield \u2022\u2022, Ward \u2022\u2022, Armor of the Soul \u2022\u2022\u2022, Ephemeral Wall \u2022\u2022\u2022, Bind Spirit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Pocket Realm \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Dead Zone \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Hide Space \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></li> <li><b><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Conjuration </span></i></b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">- Influence Heat \u2022, Magnify* \u2022, Apportation \u2022\u2022, Influence Electricity \u2022\u2022, Control Fire \u2022\u2022\u2022, Portal \u2022\u2022\u2022, Phantasmal Weapon \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Thunderbolt \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Create Hollow \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Radiation \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></li> <li><b><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Transmutation </span></i></b><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">- </span></i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Alter Conductivity \u2022, Receiver \u2022, Transmute Liquid \u2022\u2022, Transform Aura \u2022\u2022, Create Tass \u2022\u2022\u2022, Transmute Earth \u2022\u2022\u2022, Siphon Integrity \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Transmute Gold \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Forge Thaumium \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Greater Transmogrification \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sobriquet</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Sages</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Spellcasting Examples: </span></b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mnerva, a specialist in the Sphere of Conjuration, possesses a pair of white silk gloves. Close inspection reveals that the fingers are stitched with silver sigils. When worn with paired sapphire rings, also etched with miniscule runes, Mnerva can fling brightly colored lightning from her fingertips.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ivan Blackthorne appears a normal man, but were he to remove his shirt you would see tattooed upon his chest an elaborate rune circle. These runes, symbolic of the Sphere of Transmutation, act as a shortcut to oblation. Ivan need only hold a piece of tass to the circle and the mana within is drawn into his pattern.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Tanis Alcavan requires gold for a rune array, but not just any gold, liquid gold that will never freeze. Creating it is a two step process; first he inscribes a furnace, inside and out, with runes of transmutation. Then he does the same to a black iron crucible. In the crucible he places a piece of lead, which in turn goes into the fire. Tanis fills the the runes of the furnace with mana, transmuting the led to gold, then the runes of the crucible, insuring that the gold will remain liquid until it's purpose is served.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Odis Sed has just purchased his very first sanctum, a great fortress of an estate which he now must ward. Odis takes a woodworking chisel and goes to every door and window in the house, carving on the frame of each an identical ring of runes. In the basement, at the dead center of the home, he inscribes a spiral circle to act as the symbolic 'control center' of the spell. His task complete Odis then goes about wallpapering the entire estate to hide the now luminescent runes.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Terry is in deep, he flaunted his magic openly and earned the attention of a pair of witch hunters. Now he's trapped in a warehouse, rushed and without his tools. All he has to work with is a piece of chalk, not the ideal material with which to construct and array, but he'll take what he can get. To buy time Terry locks himself in the foreman\u2019s office and marks the door with the five runes of summer, super-heating the handle. But that'll do little good of the hunters just smash their way in, so he also sketches runes along the outside of the frame with lines leading to a circle at the center of the door, making the fragile wood diamond tough. </span></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-08-2013, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T03:29:10-08:00","id":6714,"title":"","content":"Nicely done.<br /> <br /> If I understand correctly. It's Intelligence + Academics for Minerva to craft her gloves and rings, then Intelligence + Conjuration for her to throw a bolt of lightning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T12:21:27-08:00","id":6965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=6714#post6714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nicely done.<br /> <br /> If I understand correctly. It's Intelligence + Academics for Minerva to craft her gloves and rings, then Intelligence + Conjuration for her to throw a bolt of lightning?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd example would be one of those cases I'd advise a GM just wave the roll. Carefully embroidered gloves would take days to make and couldn't really be replicated in a scene (not to say Lightning Flinging couldn't be cast through a different presentation). The Chalk example is better one for rolling Intelligence + Academics first, I'll clarify this in doc. Good feedback <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:37:49-08:00","id":10434,"title":"","content":"Damn I like this stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T16:01:54-08:00","id":10857,"title":"","content":"Creating Proximi, Quiescence: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">...their magic is associated with the supernatural and remains subject to Quiescence. Mortals will rapidly forget and explain away encounters with Proximi just as they do supernatural magic.</span></span></span>&quot; Did you mean &quot;Supernal&quot;? Saying magic is associated with the supernatural is kind of a pleonasm: of course magic is supernatural. Supernal, however, (as in &quot;the Supernal Realms, etc.) is specifically used to refer to Awakened magic and its source, and thus is linked to the vulnerability to Quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T16:16:27-08:00","id":10875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=10857#post10857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating Proximi, Quiescence: &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">...their magic is associated with the supernatural and remains subject to Quiescence. Mortals will rapidly forget and explain away encounters with Proximi just as they do supernatural magic.</span></span></span>&quot; Did you mean &quot;Supernal&quot;? Saying magic is associated with the supernatural is kind of a pleonasm: of course magic is supernatural. Supernal, however, (as in &quot;the Supernal Realms, etc.) is specifically used to refer to Awakened magic and its source, and thus is linked to the vulnerability to Quiescence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes I did. Good catch. Changed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T16:33:51-08:00","id":10897,"title":"","content":"There are some other uses of the word &quot;supernatural&quot; in the document which might be mistakes. A word search might be appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T12:29:15-08:00","id":16228,"title":"","content":"Quick question I'm hoping someone can answer (because I don't have access to my books at the moment): What book are magical styles detailed in? And what is the page number on which they start?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T12:45:34-08:00","id":16236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=16228#post16228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question I'm hoping someone can answer (because I don't have access to my books at the moment): What book are magical styles detailed in? And what is the page number on which they start?</div> </div> </div> </div>Magical Styles are covered in the Chronicler's Guide, page 110.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T03:12:42-08:00","id":16551,"title":"","content":"It is done! After weeks of setbacks, some sickness, writers, block and two ground up rewrites Thaumaturges are finally in a presentable state!<br /> <br /> They may be viewed here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11HySDVBaLtKQgEVMOX3SHVBJmEk4XmRqPntwMctxbuo/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...wMctxbuo/edit#</a><br /> <br /> Now, mind you the document isn't totally complete. There are still two more Colleges I want to add (The Qi Gong, martial artists who form Sorceries via Kata. And a yet unnamed group of reapers who draw their magic from stolen human souls). As always I'll also be touching things up based on feedback, so comment away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-23-2013, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T04:22:51-08:00","id":16567,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... Protagonist is learning magic at a College, happy to be surrounded by people enthusiastic about the arcane arts. Surprise twist! The director is part of a society of super-powerful sorcerers who only maintain the College as a way to study an inferior kind of magic!<br /> <br /> Sounds like a novel that needs to be written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T15:07:18-08:00","id":17328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=16567#post16567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... Protagonist is learning magic at a College, happy to be surrounded by people enthusiastic about the arcane arts. Surprise twist! The director is part of a society of super-powerful sorcerers who only maintain the College as a way to study an inferior kind of magic!<br /> <br /> Sounds like a novel that needs to be written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh duh, it was written. It's called <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Worst_Witch\" target=\"_blank\">The Worst Witch</a>. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T15:32:12-08:00","id":17339,"title":"","content":"Wait what?!<br /> <br /> I loved those books as a kid, but I don't remember any super-powerful sorcerers. (Admitedly I only got up to all at sea)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T16:17:34-08:00","id":17366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=17339#post17339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what?!<br /> <br /> I loved those books as a kid, but I don't remember any super-powerful sorcerers. (Admitedly I only got up to all at sea)</div> </div> </div> </div>My primary exposure was the made for TV movie, featuring Tim Curry as The Grand Wizard.<br /> <br /> Here's the highlight, thought it's not for the faint of loins: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-FMf8ltkCgM\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-FMf8ltkCgM</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T10:00:25-08:00","id":17773,"title":"","content":"Hey PenDragon, (LOOK, I assume)<br /> Stylistic point--You might want to use the Mage-standard terms here: &quot;Sleepers&quot; vs. &quot;Mages&quot; or &quot;the Awakened&quot; rather than &quot;mortals.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-25T16:07:42-08:00","id":17996,"title":"","content":"I quite enjoyed reading your new Thaumaturgy document. The multi-Arcana sphere system reminded me a little of the magic system in Hunter: Witchfinders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T00:37:35-08:00","id":18248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey PenDragon, (LOOK, I assume)<br /> Stylistic point--You might want to use the Mage-standard terms here: &quot;Sleepers&quot; vs. &quot;Mages&quot; or &quot;the Awakened&quot; rather than &quot;mortals.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume correctly. I'll take another pass and see what I can change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=17996#post17996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I quite enjoyed reading your new Thaumaturgy document. The multi-Arcana sphere system reminded me a little of the magic system in Hunter: Witchfinders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I plunged through just about every minor magic approach in nWoD trying to get inspiration for this, so it's not a surprise. Though the core of their inspiration draws from Ascension, and its looser, more paradigmatic casting. Glad you liked it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T01:27:18-08:00","id":18279,"title":"","content":"You say Hollow a lot. It's Hallow.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturges can recover Mana more easily than Proximi (they have the option of oblation with no Hallow), but they do NOT have a mandatory cost of 1 mana per spell like Proximi? This is intended?<br /> <br /> How big, at a minimum, does an object have to be to bear the runes necessary for a spell? If I can put one spell on each bead of my necklace, that makes for a different situation than if I have to use the whole necklace for a single runic array.<br /> <br /> When a channeler uses the Rite of Union, how much control does the possessing entity have? Tombeaux's example shows that he can exorcise or seal himself, so obviously he can use magic against the ghost's wish, but it also mentions the spirit using his body for &quot;cruel deeds&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T01:48:09-08:00","id":18295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18279#post18279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say Hollow a lot. It's Hallow.<br /> <br /> Thaumaturges can recover Mana more easily than Proximi (they have the option of oblation with no Hallow), but they do NOT have a mandatory cost of 1 mana per spell like Proximi? This is intended?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed both of these. Sorceries should cost 1 mana each.<br /> <br /> I've also been considering making it a bit easier for Proximi to recover mana. As in practice running out of Mana and not being able to get it back is the death of fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18279#post18279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How big, at a minimum, does an object have to be to bear the runes necessary for a spell? If I can put one spell on each bead of my necklace, that makes for a different situation than if I have to use the whole necklace for a single runic array.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's on the Storyteller, but as a rule of thumb the bigger the spell the more elaborate the array has to be. So while I'm all for using a necklace to support an array, each bead would be pushing it, at least at my table (perhaps if they were all one dot Sorceries).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18279#post18279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a channeler uses the Rite of Union, how much control does the possessing entity have? Tombeaux's example shows that he can exorcise or seal himself, so obviously he can use magic against the ghost's wish, but it also mentions the spirit using his body for &quot;cruel deeds&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was gonna point to GMC, but the condition there is a little more restrictive than I'd like. So instead I added a sidebar. Long story short, a Channeller can fight for control over his own body and buy time before the spirit takes over. Once it does he is a prisoner, though lucid through the experience (a storyteller might allow a possessed Channeller to astral project for help...or attempt to possess something else, assuming he has the Sorceries for it).<br /> <br /> All good notes. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T19:06:07-08:00","id":18875,"title":"","content":"Okay I just read the Thaumturgy doc, even putting down the Embeds chapter of Demon to do so! Once again these are great! This Half Awake Project of yours I would easily pay for if it was a hardcover, it is pretty much so much condensed awesome!<br /> <br /> I really like your system, and the concept rituals is a really cool flavor for all the colleges. I totally feel like I should replace the 2nd sight rules with this now!<br /> <br /> So if I read this right a Mesmerist doesn't need to be in a trance if the sorceries are cast on a patient in a trance?<br /> <br /> May I recommend Magical Armor added to the Suggestion sphere, its a classic effect of mind over matter. I remember the first time Spiderman teamed up with Doctor Strange a Sorcerer Mesmerised two common thugs into not feeling pain and they were thus able to punch through wood and shrug off blows from Spidey aimed at what he thought were normal people. Not to mention the whole mesmerize an audience member into picking up a coal trick.<br /> <br /> My suggestion on character Creation is to give 3 spheres to a starting character for them to divide among their College's spheres, with the stipulation that they must have one dot in at least two different spheres. This broadens the variety of starting Thaumaturgists, while preventing the min-maxing issue of putting all your spheres points into one sphere. It also allows for Sorcerers who aren't keen on one of the three College spheres. There is a lot of potential to be had with playing with assumptions, such as making a male oracle with no dots in Augury.<br /> <br /> I love the way channelers are done because it allows me to handle shamans, houngans, and unlikely mediums all using one system. And I think they would make for great potential Sin Eaters! When they become Bound you could even pretty much use the same system for them Awakening as Mages! Their Familiars/Mentor/whatevers could even become their Geist, with them digivolving from Ghosts/Spirits into Geists at singular moments of Emergency. Hell they could even just be Geists to begin with. I do appreciate that Geist origins are kept a mystery for the ST to exploit in ways such as this.<br /> <br /> <br /> So how did the Scholars of Urd choose their name? Was it because of their Rune Study and the prominence of Runes in Norse Magic? I guess because they were the first you created they have the quintessential feel for the whole project in their history.<br /> <br /> <br /> I recommend dumping the Hedge Wizard Title, Both Sorcerer and Thaumaturgist feels like a much stronger/more appropriate title. Hedge Wizard is a very resonant name, but it feels like it should be something else. Hell we need something than uses the title wizard eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T23:47:29-08:00","id":18981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18875#post18875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I just read the Thaumturgy doc, even putting down the Embeds chapter of Demon to do so! Once again these are great! This Half Awake Project of yours I would easily pay for if it was a hardcover, it is pretty much so much condensed awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardcover, man if only. Though when all five parts are done I might try to get it all in a neatly formatted PDF, assuming I can find someone who can show me how to do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18875#post18875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like your system, and the concept rituals is a really cool flavor for all the colleges. I totally feel like I should replace the 2nd sight rules with this now!</div> </div> </div> </div> I drew a lot from Second Sight while writing this, in fact reading through Second Sight prompted my first ground up rewrite. One of the goals was to make it possible to execute many of the concepts there through this new system. I'm glad you think that's doable.<br /> <br /> Now onto notes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18875#post18875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I read this right a Mesmerist doesn't need to be in a trance if the sorceries are cast on a patient in a trance?<br /> <br /> <br /> May I recommend Magical Armor added to the Suggestion sphere, its a classic effect of mind over matter. I remember the first time Spiderman teamed up with Doctor Strange a Sorcerer Mesmerised two common thugs into not feeling pain and they were thus able to punch through wood and shrug off blows from Spidey aimed at what he thought were normal people. Not to mention the whole mesmerize an audience member into picking up a coal trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo on the patient in trance thing. All credit to TKR for that idea.<br /> <br /> As for magical armor, I hadn't thought of that, and probably won't include it as an example (because it takes a bit of explaining). But don't let that stop you, the Sorcery lists are just suggestions after all to get the brain churning. Spheres should be viewed very broadly, perhaps even more so than Arcana, and should enable players to execute the concepts they desire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18875#post18875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion on character Creation is to give 3 spheres to a starting character for them to divide among their College's spheres, with the stipulation that they must have one dot in at least two different spheres. This broadens the variety of starting Thaumaturgists, while preventing the min-maxing issue of putting all your spheres points into one sphere. It also allows for Sorcerers who aren't keen on one of the three College spheres. There is a lot of potential to be had with playing with assumptions, such as making a male oracle with no dots in Augury.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good suggestion, I will do this. In fact I just did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18875#post18875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the way channelers are done because it allows me to handle shamans, houngans, and unlikely mediums all using one system. And I think they would make for great potential Sin Eaters! When they become Bound you could even pretty much use the same system for them Awakening as Mages! Their Familiars/Mentor/whatevers could even become their Geist, with them digivolving from Ghosts/Spirits into Geists at singular moments of Emergency. Hell they could even just be Geists to begin with. I do appreciate that Geist origins are kept a mystery for the ST to exploit in ways such as this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Channelers actually started out as Houngan, but I couldn't find a way to condense the incredibly varied art of Voodoo (which is all the hell over the place style wise) into one College. So I went the opposite direct and made a College into which certain aspects of Voodoo could be folded. Geist certainly came to mind while writing it, I almost referenced them, but I curtailed it since this is supposed to be accessible with the Core Mage book and nothing more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18875#post18875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how did the Scholars of Urd choose their name? Was it because of their Rune Study and the prominence of Runes in Norse Magic? I guess because they were the first you created they have the quintessential feel for the whole project in their history.</div> </div> </div> </div>They got their name from Ur\u00f0arbrunnr (the Well of Urd). In legend Odin, the Norse god, discovered runes by staring into the well of Urd while he hung dying from Yggdrasil. The Scholars took the name because it closely mirrored their own experiences (and perhaps a little hubris in comparing themselves to the All-Father). They and the Houngans were the first two I came up with, and were the guiding model off which I based the Thaumaturgy structure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18875#post18875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend dumping the Hedge Wizard Title, Both Sorcerer and Thaumaturgist feels like a much stronger/more appropriate title. Hedge Wizard is a very resonant name, but it feels like it should be something else. Hell we need something than uses the title wizard eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I'd dumped it completely, but I'll have to go back and look. Regardless you are right, Thaumaturge and Sorcerer are better terms to describe these casters. (I almost game the Scholars of Urd the nickname &quot;Wizards&quot; but decided that might cause some confusion).<br /> <br /> Anyway thanks for reading, glad to know you liked it. If you spot any other problems, have more questions, or get an idea you really want to contribute, ask away. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Also, I tweaked Proximi a bit as well. They now recover 1 mana a day, assuming they've had time to relax and sleep. No longer will players be hung out to dry without a hallow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-27-2013, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T13:56:16-08:00","id":19339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=18981#post18981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Also, I tweaked Proximi a bit as well. They now recover 1 mana a day, assuming they've had time to relax and sleep. No longer will players be hung out to dry without a hallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes for the strange situation that a Mage could keep Proximi around as sources of Mana, and that Proximi actually lose some of their access to Mana if they Awaken (though they do get the ability to cast spells for free). Just wanted to make sure you realized this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T15:01:51-08:00","id":19368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=19339#post19339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes for the strange situation that a Mage could keep Proximi around as sources of Mana, and that Proximi actually lose some of their access to Mana if they Awaken (though they do get the ability to cast spells for free). Just wanted to make sure you realized this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages keeping Proximi for Mana seems niche enough that I wouldn't change anything to stop it. There are, after all, easier ways to get mana than sucking it from other casters.<br /> <br /> The second is a bit of a concern, but hopefully corrected by the fact that all Awakened Proximi end up in a Legacy, and can therefore perform oblations without a hallow. So neither really concern me that much, not in the grand scheme of things at least. Still, good to keep in mind. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T16:19:17-08:00","id":19415,"title":"","content":"Added a new College, Qigong Masters. Your standard martial monks with mystical powers. If you are after Wuxia, element bending mystics, or looking to recreate the Big Trouble in Little China* their the way to go.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Seriously though, if you want to recreate Big Trouble, use Ascension. The vibe there is so right.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Edit: Tweaked Spheres a bit to use terms more appropriate to the inspirations.</span></b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-27-2013, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T18:09:02-08:00","id":24088,"title":"","content":"Yet another Thaumaturgy update: Added the Nephesh Heresy, a left-handed College of reapers who use human souls to fuel their arts. Unaffiliated with the Mysterium the Nephesh are maintained by Tremere Lich Houses, who use mortal reapers as fronts to harvest human souls. Need a classic evil wizard, dark lord, or a Hellraiser-like torture fiend? The Nephesh Heresy will do the trick.<br /> <br /> View it <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11HySDVBaLtKQgEVMOX3SHVBJmEk4XmRqPntwMctxbuo/edit#heading=h.p2uucsg0608x\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T16:52:49-08:00","id":24749,"title":"","content":"Expanded Blessings for the Proximi Line Baal's Blood, adding 8 new spells with a range of antagonistic options (demonic familiars, invisibility cloaks, infernal traps, and mind destroying hexes). <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Urxj0z6zvILm6-RAdUWXi5X_M6ppIjQ54H2Cb_prQM/edit#heading=h.1s4q4zexfiim\" target=\"_blank\">View it here</a>.<br /> <br /> Probably, gonna do the Sons of Bezalel and Skinwalker Tribes next, then onto Part 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T18:59:12-08:00","id":26897,"title":"","content":"Expanded Skinwalker Blessings. 8 more blessings as usual. On a related note, Mizaki films are great inspiration for animism.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Urxj0z6zvILm6-RAdUWXi5X_M6ppIjQ54H2Cb_prQM/edit#heading=h.frode3ug7lpl\" target=\"_blank\">View Here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T20:09:19-08:00","id":26947,"title":"","content":"Ah, come on PenDragon. Dammit. You're doing it on purpose. I was going to write all grumpy and bitter, muttering about you spending too much time writing cool stuff for Vampire, upgrading Disciplines to GM style and stuff, and you go and write Child of Gaia. Can you explain me please how i get mad and vexed at you now? Absolutely loved that. Had to tell you. Pendragon's Proximy and Qigong were so cool, but those new Blessings on Skinwalkers are really hot stuff. Congrats man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T20:13:45-08:00","id":26950,"title":"","content":"PS. Where are my full stops, Android? My phone is trolling me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:54:26-08:00","id":43737,"title":"","content":"Holidays are over and I'm back to writing.<br /> <br /> Just updated the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Urxj0z6zvILm6-RAdUWXi5X_M6ppIjQ54H2Cb_prQM/edit#heading=h.24vbknn3cza4\" target=\"_blank\">Sons of Bezalel</a>, they received a slightly more extensive modification than the other lines. I changed up their Arcana and altered their Sobriquet. There are some guidelines for statting Golems, though the process remains very open ended. And of course there are 8 new spells, filling out the Bezalel options with a bit of necromancy, spontaneous animation, a variety of Golem enhancing magics, and the T10,000 (as in Terminator).<br /> <br /> Imbued are up next, though they're still a ways off. B&amp;S really pulled my mind away from Mage, but it's finding its way back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T15:10:30-08:00","id":44465,"title":"","content":"So I now had a spare moment to read these, on the whole I like the concept and the theme; but I couldn't help but feel that they were harmed by being fit into a generic Proximi mechanical structure. The way their spells work felt clunky. Designing a system specifically for golem crafting (or steal and modify Automata from Genius) would be a big improvement in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:02:14-08:00","id":44502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=44465#post44465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I now had a spare moment to read these, on the whole I like the concept and the theme; but I couldn't help but feel that they were harmed by being fit into a generic Proximi mechanical structure. The way their spells work felt clunky. Designing a system specifically for golem crafting (or steal and modify Automata from Genius) would be a big improvement in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI have, on the whole, favored a somewhat system light approach for this project, which is most evident in the Bezalel. Mostly I wanted to make sure that there wasn't a lot of humming and hawing over dice pools and mechanical minutia, so I'm putting trust that a storyteller and player can come to an agreement on what both feel are appropriate stats for a Golem. <br /> <br /> A unique system of automata design would indeed be nice, but that'd be a completely separate project, and I wanted a family of Golem crafters. So, there you have it. Of course if you have a clean, compatible alternative I am all ears. It's a work in progress after all.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:30:20-08:00","id":44525,"title":"","content":"Wwwoh. The Thaumaturgy part was...superb. Too long to read in depht for tonight, but definitely looking very good. I don't know if I like the &quot;they aren't Second Sight traditions&quot; but anyway, a really good work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:41:36-08:00","id":44535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=19368#post19368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages keeping Proximi for Mana seems niche enough that I wouldn't change anything to stop it. There are, after all, easier ways to get mana than sucking it from other casters.<br /> <br /> The second is a bit of a concern, but hopefully corrected by the fact that all Awakened Proximi end up in a Legacy, and can therefore perform oblations without a hallow. So neither really concern me that much, not in the grand scheme of things at least. Still, good to keep in mind. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just Attribute scour every day for 3 mana. It's not an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T09:22:53-08:00","id":44939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=44525#post44525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wwwoh. The Thaumaturgy part was...superb. Too long to read in depht for tonight, but definitely looking very good. I don't know if I like the &quot;they aren't Second Sight traditions&quot; but anyway, a really good work.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, what do you mean by &quot;they aren't second sight traditions&quot;? The Thaumaturges here were designed to work with Awakening, both socially and mechanically, and be associated with the Mysterium (because all groups in this project associate with one of the orders). If that's not your thing then it's quite easy to remove the awakened connection and use Colleges as stand alone organizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T09:15:42-08:00","id":48221,"title":"","content":"Thumbs up on PenDragon keep on writing this! (I'm so looking forward to the Imbued and the Occulted -not to dismiss Technomancy, but i'm not big fan of The Free Council- ).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T03:54:08-08:00","id":73124,"title":"","content":"Great work here! I read both splats and am pretty impressed with it - it's just THAT MUCH BETTER for interpretation of lesser magic then Second Sight and even WItch Finders. And it opens so many interpretations and possibilities - from classic hedge witches with cauldrons and mages who cast spells through some gibberish language to Jacky Estacado's Darkness and Harry Potter wand-casters. Thanks for it.<br /> <br /> And i also have a few questions and possible suggestions:<br /> <br /> 1) Are Urd's magic arrays onetime thing or is it possible for these guys to go around with spell-books with all their fancy magics needing only to be charged? Cause Spellcasting examples and &quot;<b>This Land Is My Land&quot; </b>give somehow different approaches.<br /> <br /> 2) There is notion, that ST may include other Sphers into College's purview, but is it possible for thaumaturge to get access to other Spheres through his practice? Something along the line of studying out-of-clan Disciplines and old Mages' &quot;not specialized&quot; Spheres.<br /> <br /> 3) Following previous point: is it possible to cast foreign Spheres through frame of another Colledge's Ritual? Something like thaumaturge, who has some degree of familiarity with both Scholars of Urd and Wayfarer's Society using later's mind control through his runes.<br /> <br /> 4) Did You consider adding some kinds of &quot;special magic maneuvers&quot; to different Colledges? Something along the line of Scholars of Urd creating onetime-use rune arrays for getting more power for this particular spell (die bonus), but with that write-up losing all its reality-altering weight for later uses; the Warlock going for a certain break of usurped soul to get more power right here, right now - automatic loss of integrity in Phylactery in addition to following roll which provides bonus for spellcasting; skipping the ritual part completely - Scholar visualizes his rune array, Monk remembers the feeling of thousands used katas, etc - at the cost of penalty to the cating roll (spell level or double of it, probably).<br /> <br /> 5) Did You consider following in footsteps of V:tM Thaumaturgy &amp; V:tR Blood Sorcery and having more generalized rating of &quot;[Colledge name] Style Mastery&quot; in addition to Spheres' levels? It would give clear idea of thaumaturge's general proficiency in particular form of Art and could be used to determine other advantages, or something. Like, having the guy with 4 score in Style, through which he performs magic right now, casting level 1 spell and giving him 3 die bonus on the roll; or the guy who has &quot;Urd Mastery&quot; rating of 3 and &quot;Sibilines Mastery&quot; of 1 (with appropriate Sphere) cast the later's spell through the frame of first's ritual, cause he is just that much better in it, etc.<br /> <br /> 6) Did You consider giving to thaumaturges Supernatural Advantage? Synthetic one, but still. Something like having special merit rated from 1 to [highest Sphere] (or Mastery from my previous suggestion), which should be specifically bought up to that level and having thaumaturge to take care of it in particularly appropriate way. Something like Scholar having some kind of runic necklace, on which he has to scribe new runes on each day or it will deteriorate; or Guru having to tend to some kind of fetish-like thing. Maybe it should be expressed in the form having to spend Mana to charge the thing each day, or it'll drop down to zero point after some time, until thaumaturge charges it enough again (max is his permanent rating in merit); or probably it'll deteriorate after actually being used - like contesting supernatural power; or probably it may be used as additional mana storage - up to its rating points, or something.<br /> <br /> P.S. Am I right in expecting imbued to be somehow similar to Corvo from &quot;Dishonored&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2156-overbound","user":"Overbound","date":". 02-16-2014, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2156-overbound","name":"Overbound","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T12:37:44-08:00","id":74467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overbound</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=73124#post73124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great work here! I read both splats and am pretty impressed with it - it's just THAT MUCH BETTER for interpretation of lesser magic then Second Sight and even WItch Finders. And it opens so many interpretations and possibilities - from classic hedge witches with cauldrons and mages who cast spells through some gibberish language to Jacky Estacado's Darkness and Harry Potter wand-casters. Thanks for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, glad to hear it! Thaumaturgy took a long time to come together (like, 3-4 major revisions), but the outcome was worth the headache.<br /> <br /> Now, to answers:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overbound</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=73124#post73124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Are Urd's magic arrays onetime thing or is it possible for these guys to go around with spell-books with all their fancy magics needing only to be charged? Cause Spellcasting examples and &quot;<b>This Land Is My Land&quot; </b>give somehow different approaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>An array can be used as many times as a Sage pleases. Spellbooks, engraved relics, reusable summoning circles and occult tattoos are all common of the Scholars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overbound</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=73124#post73124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) There is notion, that ST may include other Spheres into College's purview, but is it possible for thaumaturge to get access to other Spheres through his practice? Something along the line of studying out-of-clan Disciplines and old Mages' &quot;not specialized&quot; Spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturges may research and invent new Spheres, with storyteller approval of course. You could invent a Divination Sphere for the Scholars of Urd, or a Necromancy sphere for the Wayfarers, etc. Research and discovery is the name of the Thaumaturgy game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overbound</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=73124#post73124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Following previous point: is it possible to cast foreign Spheres through frame of another Colledge's Ritual? Something like thaumaturge, who has some degree of familiarity with both Scholars of Urd and Wayfarer's Society using later's mind control through his runes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sphere's aren't definitive things like Arcana. They are broad wrappers Mages use for a variety of spells that fit a certain theme. So no, a Thaumturge cannot improvise spells of a different College to fit their own, not without completely reinventing them (i.e. buying the spell again in a different College). This is why cross College Thaumaturges are so rare, it's a lot of work without a whole lot of benefit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overbound</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=73124#post73124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Did You consider adding some kinds of &quot;special magic maneuvers&quot; to different Colledges? Something along the line of Scholars of Urd creating onetime-use rune arrays for getting more power for this particular spell (die bonus), but with that write-up losing all its reality-altering weight for later uses; the Warlock going for a certain break of usurped soul to get more power right here, right now - automatic loss of integrity in Phylactery in addition to following roll which provides bonus for spellcasting; skipping the ritual part completely - Scholar visualizes his rune array, Monk remembers the feeling of thousands used katas, etc - at the cost of penalty to the cating roll (spell level or double of it, probably).</div> </div> </div> </div>Skipping the ritual is a no no. The ritual is integral to Thaumaturgy, the only way to skip it would be, well, Awakening. (Awakened Thaumaturges are likely to cast in the manner you described).<br /> <br /> Everything else there sounds pretty cool, but for the interest of simplicity I don't want to be adding a whole bunch of fiddly bonus mechanics. But that shouldn't stop you from using them at your table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overbound</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=73124#post73124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) Did You consider following in footsteps of V:tM Thaumaturgy &amp; V:tR Blood Sorcery and having more generalized rating of &quot;[Colledge name] Style Mastery&quot; in addition to Spheres' levels? It would give clear idea of thaumaturge's general proficiency in particular form of Art and could be used to determine other advantages, or something. Like, having the guy with 4 score in Style, through which he performs magic right now, casting level 1 spell and giving him 3 die bonus on the roll; or the guy who has &quot;Urd Mastery&quot; rating of 3 and &quot;Sibilines Mastery&quot; of 1 (with appropriate Sphere) cast the later's spell through the frame of first's ritual, cause he is just that much better in it, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't really considered it, no. Mostly because it's not the default assumption that a Thaumaturge will be a member of several Colleges. (Seriously, just learning the magic of one College is \u200bhumongously demanding). If you did end up needing to track it I'd go by the highest Sphere in a given College. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overbound</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=73124#post73124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) Did You consider giving to thaumaturges Supernatural Advantage? Synthetic one, but still. Something like having special merit rated from 1 to [highest Sphere] (or Mastery from my previous suggestion), which should be specifically bought up to that level and having thaumaturge to take care of it in particularly appropriate way. Something like Scholar having some kind of runic necklace, on which he has to scribe new runes on each day or it will deteriorate; or Guru having to tend to some kind of fetish-like thing. Maybe it should be expressed in the form having to spend Mana to charge the thing each day, or it'll drop down to zero point after some time, until thaumaturge charges it enough again (max is his permanent rating in merit); or probably it'll deteriorate after actually being used - like contesting supernatural power; or probably it may be used as additional mana storage - up to its rating points, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considered yes. I was originally going to give all of them Supernatural Advantages, but was convinced otherwise. This is, after all, supposed to be about mortals who've attained magic through other means (Proximi get a pass specifically because they're <b>not </b>normal). <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean Thaumaturges are defenseless. Every College has at least one Sphere that can be spun in a defensive manner (i.e. Mage Armor), and a variety of magical options for self defense. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Overbound</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=73124#post73124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S. Am I right in expecting imbued to be somehow similar to Corvo from &quot;Dishonored&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a reasonable inspiration source of inspiration, yes. Though they're slightly less grab baggy in their abilities.<br /> <br /> Ah, what the hell, a little spoiler:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Imbued are Sleepwalkers who have their souls tampered with to give them a small set of innate powers. The Adamant Arrow is largely responsible for the practice, using it as a way to give zealous acolytes a way to &quot;get in the fight&quot; and contend with Supernal forces.</li> <li>Imbued are grouped into Brotherhoods, each with a creed and purpose. As a part of the Imbuing process they are given a Geas, a compulsion to make certain they don't stray from their intended path.</li> <li>Mechanically Imbued are essentially humans with a Legacy. They possess Attainments (called Investments) that can be called upon at will. Compared to Proximi and Thaumaturges Imbued are very specialized, possessing great expertise in an extremely narrow field. However, they have the advantage of being able to grow rapidly in power, and access their Investments with little risk. (i.e. Investments are free to use, and not subject to dispelling or disbelief.)</li> <li>Imbued can also purchase enchantments, which represent spells Awakened Mages have cast into them, much like Imbuing an item. They can use they're limited internal Mana reserves to activate these abilities, though they require the assistance of Mages to recharge them.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T09:13:26-08:00","id":75664,"title":"","content":"Hmm, questions. Can a scholar of Urd use another scholar's array? In more detail: Can you steal and use an array whenever you get your greedy hands on them? Can you create an array specifically for someone else's use? Can you make an array as a collaborative effort for the both of you to use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T10:27:46-08:00","id":75726,"title":"","content":"Q: Can a scholar of Urd use another scholar's array?<br /> A: Yes. Though I'd require an Intelligence + Relevant Sphere roll, penalized by the Array's Sphere Rating, to figure out how the devil it works.<br /> <br /> Q: Can you steal and use an array whenever you get your greedy hands on them?<br /> A: Hell yes.<br /> <br /> Q: Can you create an array specifically for someone else's use?<br /> A: Sure. See Answer #1 for deciphering roll.<br /> <br /> Q: Can you make an array as a collaborative effort for the both of you to use?<br /> A: Absolutely, assuming both Sages know the spell in question. (Though a Sage could also hand out blue-prints to his apprentices and have them lay the groundwork).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T10:22:23-08:00","id":82148,"title":"","content":"I have a question. Isn\u00b4t the Telyavel curse too much...demanding? a fix of magical blood per day (not to mention how hard can be to find a vampire or werewolf as &quot; willing donor&quot;), while ghouls only need 1 vitae per month to keep going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T13:25:31-08:00","id":82273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=82148#post82148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question. Isn\u00b4t the Telyavel curse too much...demanding? a fix of magical blood per day (not to mention how hard can be to find a vampire or werewolf as &quot; willing donor&quot;), while ghouls only need 1 vitae per month to keep going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every day is pretty steep. I'll tweak it to a week.<br /> <br /> Note though that the Telyavel have a Blessing that dramatically reduces the severity of their curse, Red Tass. So even in the absence of other magical beings young Telyavel can rely on their elders for their &quot;fix&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Tweaked it further. Telyavel can now survive on mundane blood just fine, day by day. Magic blood is more sustaining, staying their curse for a week, instead of a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-01-2014, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T15:44:04-07:00","id":108677,"title":"","content":"&quot;What's this? I thought this project was abandoned,&quot; they say.<br /> <br /> &quot;He hasn't updated in so long he's most certainly forgotten,&quot; they think<br /> <br /> But no, as it turns out I was just overworked and mentally exhausted. Take that fictional naysayers!<br /> <br /> Now I'm back to hacking at the Imbued, Sleepwalkers invested with legacy like powers by rare sub-sects of the Adamant Arrow. The Imbued draw their inspiration from comics and super heroes, rare humans imbued with narrow abilities and higher purpose. And while the project is still quite incomplete I am at the stage where a little feedback will go a long way. Mind you what I'm spoiling is a bit out of context, so I'll try to breakdown the mechanical bits left out:<ul><li>Investments are free, and often permanently active. They cannot be dispelled, are not affected by quiessence or disbelief, and cannot be suppressed by any means other than the Imbued Geas (see spoiler)</li> <li>Enchantments cost 1 Mana to activate for a scene. They are awakened magic and therefore suffer quiessence, disbelief and dispelling. However, they cannot be removed from an Imbued completely without Prime 5, only suppressed until reactivated.</li> </ul>Spoilers ahoy:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:32px\">Heirs to Olympus</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Origins: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Borne in ancient Greece, even before the height of its power, Heirs to Olympus are founded on a singular philosophy; for man to rise to the challenges beyond this world, they must first rise to those within it. To this end the Brotherhood sought to gather and empower the finest of humanity. Generals, artists, philosophers and explorers. Throughout history stood Paragons whose legends continue to inspire to this day, and though not all of history's great luminaries were Paragons, all Paragons are luminaries.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Recruitment: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">To inspire man a Paragon must lead by example. In a world dominated by symbols of submission, this is a daunting task. The Heirs to Olympus pick from only the most exemplary to join their campaign, looking for force of will, clear vision, and a larger than life presence. Of course that means most Paragons are extremely driven towards causes of their own, but that suits the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Heirs to Olympus</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> just fine. So long as a Paragon continues to fearlessly inspire others to stand for themselves against corruption, it doesn't really matter what specific cause he is trumpeting.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Once selected a prospective Paragon must submit herself to a series of grueling trials, designed to test her every facet physically, mentally, and spiritually. Though she is never informed of this during the trial, the potential Paragon needn't succeed in every task, but she must show an enduring spirit and a drive to overcome each obstacle. Any sign of backing down is grounds for dismissal. At the end of the gauntlet the sleepwalker emerges spiritually prepared for the final ritual. She is brought to a secret ruin and blessed in an enchanted pool, emerging a Paragon for all humanity to see.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Geas: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As a paragon of humanity </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Heirs to Olympus</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> mustn\u2019t show weakness or debauchery. Whenever a Prodigal Son gives into his vice he loses access to his Investment for the rest of the scene. Whenever he fails a breaking point he loses access to his Investments for a full day.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Enchantments: </span></b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Heirs to Olympus</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> favor personal enchantments rooted firmly in the material. They empower a Paragon directly as the Brotherhood\u2019s creed outright forbids the use of magic to directly influence or affect humanity, but a gentle nudge is generally acceptable. Mind, Life, and Fate are the most common Arcana, while Death and Spirit are rare.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Common Enchantments: Winds of Chance \u2022\u2022, One Mind Two Thoughts \u2022\u2022, Alter Aura \u2022\u2022\u2022, Fortune\u2019s Protection \u2022\u2022\u2022, Augment the Mind \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Lucky Coin \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Forge Destiny \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supreme Augmentation \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Enchantment Dice Pool</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Presence + Paragon Skill (see Below)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sobriquet</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: Paragons</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Paragon Investment</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A Cut Above</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> \u2022</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Paragons represent the pinnacle of human achievement, they are the best of the best, seemly blessed with talent and gravitas. He constantly benefits from the spell </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">First Impressions</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> and never succumbs to fear, mundane or magical</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In addition, when he gains this Investment mark the Paragon\u2019s two highest ranked skills (if several are tied for highest, he picks two from among them), these become his Paragon Skills. Paragons gain 9-again on all </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">mundane </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">rolls involving their Paragon skills.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cream of the Crop \u2022\u2022</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">People look to Paragons for leadership and inspiration, and defer to them in times of need. Mortal bystanders will assume the Paragon is a figure of authority, and follow his instruction with little prompting. He increases the general impression of all mortals towards him by two steps, and reduces the number of Doors (GMC pg. 192) in Social Maneuvering by two. Finally, he gains 8-again on all rolls involving his Paragon skills.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Exemplar </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A Paragon\u2019s excellence becomes almost palpable, his presence radiant, larger than life. He seems to fill every space he enters and inspire simply with his presence. To act against such a figure seems almost unfathomable, and to many, impossible. Those who intend to act against him in any respect save self defense, must succeed a Resolve + Composure roll, penalized by his Presence. Similarly those he acts against must succeed the same roll, or give way in his presence. In addition, he gains the Rote Quality on all rolls involving his Paragon skills.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Miracle Worker </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Paragons excellence expands beyond mundane reason, presence and expertise so great as to defy reality. She may now accomplish acts using her Paragon skills that should be flat out impossible, or tremendously unlikely. Ricocheting bullets to strike hidden targets, jury-rigging functional aircraft from household implements, performing comprehensive psychoanalysis based on tiny indicators on a person\u2019s clothing, etc. Non-combat actions treat a single success as Exceptional Success, while damaging actions (like called shots) reduce penalties (including defense) by 5. Extended actions halve, rounded up, the target number and the interval between rolls. </span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 04-14-2014, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T22:24:16-07:00","id":108980,"title":"","content":"What were the Prodigal Sons originally called? And why are they called \u201cProdigal\u201d (which means \u201cwastefully extravagent\u201d)? Or \u201cSons\u201d, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T00:50:46-07:00","id":109068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/484-half-awake-awakened-magic-for-the-unawakened?p=108980#post108980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What were the Prodigal Sons originally called? And why are they called \u201cProdigal\u201d (which means \u201cwastefully extravagent\u201d)? Or \u201cSons\u201d, for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, Prodigal Sons have always had that name, but their premise shifted over so many revisions that it isn't appropriate. They originally had a big redemption theme that a trashed because 